  "live_records": {
    "q-212923": {
      "dom_id": "step-q212923",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given the relation $R$ on $N$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x>y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $6\\,R\\,8$\n- $7\\,R\\,2$\n- $9\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,1$",
      "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x>y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $>$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $≯$ (or, equivalently, $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $\\le $) are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $>,$ we have $6>8,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $>,$ we have $7>2,$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is false. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $\\le ,$ we have $9\\le 1,$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
