    "q-80860": {
      "dom_id": "step-q80860",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given the relation $R$ on $Z$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x∣(y-1),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $4\\,R\\,13$\n- $3\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,11$\n- $8\\,R\\,3$",
      "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x∣(y-1).$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. In this case, we have $4∣(13-1),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement II is true. In this case, we have $3∤(11-1),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is false. In this case, we have $8∣(3-1),$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
